---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import MediaCarousel from './MediaCarousel.astro';
import sensorCoverage from '../assets/lidar-coverage.png';
import cameraCoverage from '../assets/camera-coverage.png';
import batteryPack from '../assets/battery-pack-assembly.jpeg';
import lidarTest from '../assets/lidar-scan-test.png';
import buoyDetection from '../assets/buoy-detection.png';
import gimbalDrawing from '../assets/lidar-gimbal-drawing.png';
import batteryInBox from '../assets/battery-in-box.png';
import batteryWithBms from '../assets/battery-with-bms.png';
import batteryCellsWelded from '../assets/battery-cells-welded.png';
import frontLidarMount from '../assets/front-lidar-mount.png';
import lidarGimbalPhoto from '../assets/lidar-gimbal-photo.png';
import lidarRange12m from '../assets/lidar-range-12m.jpg';
import lidarBuoyColoured from '../assets/lidar-buoy-coloured.jpg';
import cameraViewCombined from '../assets/camera-view-combined.jpg';

const loops = [
  {
    number: '01',
    title: 'Pitch',
    body: 'The 1.8 kWh battery slides fore and aft on rails, shifting the centre of mass.',
  },
  {
    number: '02',
    title: 'Roll',
    body: 'Linear actuators in the outriggers adjust the righting moment in real time.',
  },
  {
    number: '03',
    title: 'Ride height',
    body: 'Driving both outriggers the same way lifts the main hull higher or lets it settle.',
  },
  {
    number: '04',
    title: 'Sensors',
    body: 'A custom-built gimbal holds the front lidar level through any residual motion.',
  },
];

const features = [
  {
    title: 'Pitch trim by weight shift',
    eyebrow: 'Stabilisation · Loop 01',
    images: [
      {
        video: 'pitch-only',
        width: 1280,
        height: 720,
        alt: 'The Ligmax battery sliding forward and back along its linear rails inside the hull',
        caption: 'The pitch loop on the bench — the battery running fore and aft on its rails.',
      },
    ],
    dark: true,
    body: [
      'Instead of relying on hull shape alone, Ligmax keeps itself level mechanically. The 1.8 kWh battery, the heaviest component on board, slides fore and aft on linear rails, driven by a dual-shaft stepper and belt, moving the centre of mass to trim pitch.',
      'The battery does double duty as energy store and trim mass, so the stabilisation costs almost no extra weight. The pack is notched at its forward bottom corner so it can run all the way to the front stop with part of itself sitting over the drive motor, buying travel a plain rectangular block would give up. Trimming the vessel to the right attitude to plane also cuts wetted area and drag at speed.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Roll trim by active outriggers',
    eyebrow: 'Stabilisation · Loop 02',
    images: [
      {
        video: 'tilt-only',
        width: 1280,
        height: 720,
        alt: 'The Ligmax outriggers driving up and down to counter roll',
        caption: 'The roll loop on the bench — the amas driving up and down against roll.',
      },
    ],
    dark: true,
    body: [
      'Linear actuators shift the outriggers vertically, adjusting the righting moment and the immersion of the main hull to counter roll, augmenting the passive stability of the wide trimaran stance with active control.',
      'The result is a vessel that stays composed in wake and chop, exactly when precision matters most: docking, station-keeping and threading a buoy channel.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Ride height, set on the water',
    eyebrow: 'Stabilisation · Loop 03',
    images: [
      {
        video: 'ama-height-live',
        width: 1280,
        height: 720,
        alt: 'The Ligmax outriggers driving down together to change how deep the main hull sits in the water',
        caption: 'Ride height being set while under way — both amas driving the same direction together.',
      },
    ],
    dark: true,
    body: [
      'The outriggers that fight roll also decide how deep the boat sits. Driving both actuators the same way, instead of against each other, presses the amas down and lifts the main hull clear of the water, or lets it settle back in. It is a separate axis of control sharing the same hardware as the roll loop.',
      'Ride height is set live while under way, so the vessel can be trimmed to the water it is actually on rather than to a compromise picked on shore: higher to cut wetted area and drag on a clear run, lower for a wider, steadier stance when the water is confused or when precision matters more than speed.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'A custom gimbal for the front lidar',
    eyebrow: 'Stabilisation · Loop 04',
    carousel: {
      ratio: '1 / 1',
      slides: [
        {
          image: frontLidarMount,
          alt: 'Close-up render of the gimbal-stabilised front lidar mounted in the carbon-fibre bow',
          caption: 'As designed: the gimbal carrying the 360° lidar up in the bow.',
        },
        {
          image: lidarGimbalPhoto,
          alt: 'The finished lidar gimbal mounted inside the carbon-fibre bow, photographed with the lidar lifted off',
          caption:
            'As built, with the lidar lifted off — the brushless motor underneath and the bare plate the sensor bolts onto.',
        },
      ],
    },
    dark: true,
    body: [
      'The third loop guards perception directly. The front 360° lidar rides on a compact gimbal designed and built in-house, just over 100 mm across, with its own dedicated IMU for fast, local correction. Whatever pitch and roll remain after the hull-level loops, the gimbal cancels, holding the scan plane horizontal at all times.',
      'A 2D lidar sees a single slice of the world, so that slice has to be the right one. Keeping it level means buoys stay in view scan after scan instead of vanishing as the bow lifts. That recovers the robustness of a far heavier, more expensive 3D sensor rig from an inexpensive 2D unit.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Object detection, straight from geometry',
    eyebrow: 'Sensing & autonomy',
    carousel: {
      ratio: '4 / 3',
      slides: [
        {
          image: sensorCoverage,
          alt: 'Top-down visualisation of the 360-degree lidar coverage around the vessel',
          caption: 'Two 360° lidars, one gimbal-stabilised at the bow and one aft, covering every bearing.',
        },
        {
          image: lidarRange12m,
          alt: 'Live lidar plot with returns held out near the twelve metre range ring',
          caption:
            'A live plot off the boat: returns held right out at the 12 m edge of the front lidar’s zone.',
        },
        {
          image: lidarBuoyColoured,
          alt: 'Live lidar plot showing a buoy cluster at about five metres, drawn in red',
          caption:
            'A buoy clustered out of raw scan returns at about 5 m — drawn red once the cameras have put a colour on it.',
        },
      ],
    },
    dark: true,
    body: [
      'Two 360° lidars, one gimbal-stabilised at the bow and one aft, give continuous range data on every bearing. A deterministic Euclidean clustering algorithm groups the scan returns into candidate objects, each with a range, bearing and size: fast, explainable detection with no training data required.',
      'Deterministic geometry is the backbone of a safety-critical vehicle: every detection can be traced back to the exact points that produced it.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Cameras add what lidar cannot: colour',
    eyebrow: 'Sensing & autonomy',
    carousel: {
      ratio: '2 / 1',
      slides: [
        {
          image: cameraCoverage,
          alt: 'Visualisation of the usable forward field of view of the two wide-angle cameras',
          caption: 'The usable forward arc the two 220° wide-angle cameras cover between them.',
        },
        {
          image: cameraViewCombined,
          alt: 'The two 220° camera frames joined into a single wide view of the scene in front of the boat',
          caption:
            'Both cameras at one instant, joined into a single frame: the entire forward view the boat has. The marker board sits on the seam, where the two fields overlap.',
        },
      ],
    },
    dark: true,
    body: [
      'Lidar is colour-blind, and the course is not: channel buoys are red and green. Two 220° wide-angle cameras cover the whole forward arc, and a probabilistic classifier projects each lidar detection into the camera frame and samples its colour, labelling objects without a single neural weight.',
      'As a fallback and cross-check, a YOLO26L detection network runs on dedicated vision hardware, an NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano Super, finding buoys directly in the image even in difficult light. Geometry from lidar, colour from camera, verified by the network.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'A ground station built for zero hesitation',
    eyebrow: 'Operations',
    images: [
      {
        video: 'gui-first-run',
        width: 1280,
        height: 766,
        alt: 'The Ligmax operator console tracking the vessel between buoys, with live telemetry and a plain-language readout of what the autonomy is doing',
        caption:
          'The console on the first-run data from Njord: what the boat is doing, where it is, and the reason behind every call it makes.',
      },
    ],
    dark: true,
    body: [
      'The operator console is custom software, matured on the team’s earlier 5G-controlled UGV project. A UDP hole-punched connection runs directly between vessel and laptop over 5G, with no relay or cloud in between, for the lowest latency physically achievable. It carries live camera feeds, the lidar world model and full telemetry.',
      'Picking up a game controller takes over manual control instantly, with no menus in between, and a lightweight web dashboard gives judges and team an at-a-glance view. Kill and hold commands are always one action away, mirrored on an independent long-range RC link in case 5G drops.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Resilient systems & safety',
    eyebrow: 'Engineering for the water',
    carousel: {
      ratio: '1 / 1',
      slides: [
        {
          image: batteryInBox,
          alt: 'The completed battery sealed inside its carbon-fibre enclosure, with an orange cable drag chain running off the lid',
          caption:
            'Finished: sealed into its own fireproof enclosure. The drag chain feeds power and BMS data along as the whole box slides fore and aft on its rails.',
        },
        {
          image: batteryWithBms,
          alt: 'The finished pack out of its box, wrapped in kapton with a Daly battery management system and main power leads fitted',
          caption:
            'Out of the box: wrapped, with the Daly BMS for per-cell telemetry and the main leads onto the propulsion bus.',
        },
        {
          image: batteryCellsWelded,
          alt: 'The pack with nickel strips spot-welded across the cells, before the BMS was fitted',
          caption:
            'Before the BMS — 12S12P of welded cells. The step cut out of the bottom front is deliberate: it lets the pack run to the forward stop with part of itself over the drive motor.',
        },
        {
          image: batteryPack,
          alt: 'Bare Samsung 18650 cells arranged in a block on the workbench with nickel strips laid over them, before welding',
          caption:
            'And the start of it: 144 Samsung INR18650-35E cells laid up on the bench with the nickel strips waiting to be welded.',
        },
      ],
    },
    dark: false,
    body: [
      'Safety-critical control is deliberately separated from autonomy: a Pixhawk 6C flight controller owns hard-real-time control and failsafes, while a Raspberry Pi 5 and an NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano Super run planning and perception. All propulsion power routes through a physical emergency-stop safety loop.',
      'The self-built battery lives in a fireproof aluminium-and-steel enclosure with full BMS telemetry, the hull seals with an interlocked powered lid, and three bilge pumps keep the vessel operational even after water ingress. A direct 5G link carries operator video and telemetry, with an independent long-range RC link as backup.',
    ],
  },
];

const evidence = [
  {
    image: lidarTest,
    alt: 'Live 2D lidar scan plotted during workshop testing',
    caption: 'Live lidar scan during workshop bench testing',
  },
  {
    image: buoyDetection,
    alt: 'Camera image of a green buoy on open water with a detection bounding box',
    caption: 'CNN buoy detection validated on open water',
  },
  {
    image: gimbalDrawing,
    alt: 'Technical drawing of the custom front-lidar gimbal',
    caption: 'Custom front-lidar gimbal, designed in-house',
    light: true,
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="technology">
  <div class="container">
    <div data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">Technology</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Attacking instability at the source</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Most student vessels accept wave motion and try to clean up the data in software. Ligmax handles it
        mechanically instead, with four control loops running on live sensor feedback: three that hold the
        boat and its sensors level, and one that sets how deep it rides.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="loops" data-reveal>
      {loops.map((loop) => (
        <li class="loop-card">
          <span class="loop-number">{loop.number}</span>
          <h3>{loop.title}</h3>
          <p>{loop.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="features">
      {features.map((feature, index) => (
        <article class:list={['feature', { 'feature--flip': index % 2 === 1 }]} data-reveal>
          <div class:list={['feature-media', { 'feature-media--dark': feature.dark }]}>
            {feature.carousel && (
              <MediaCarousel slides={feature.carousel.slides} ratio={feature.carousel.ratio} />
            )}
            {(feature.images ?? []).map((item) => (
              <figure class="media-figure">
                {item.video ? (
                  <video
                    class="media-video"
                    src={`/videos/${item.video}.mp4`}
                    poster={`/videos/${item.video}.jpg`}
                    width={item.width}
                    height={item.height}
                    style={`aspect-ratio: ${item.width} / ${item.height}`}
                    controls
                    loop
                    playsinline
                    preload="none"
                    aria-label={item.alt}
                  />
                ) : (
                  <Image
                    src={item.image}
                    alt={item.alt}
                    widths={[480, 720, 960]}
                    sizes="(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 520px"
                  />
                )}
                {item.caption && <figcaption>{item.caption}</figcaption>}
              </figure>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="feature-copy">
            <span class="feature-eyebrow">{feature.eyebrow}</span>
            <h3>{feature.title}</h3>
            {feature.body.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="build" data-reveal>
      <div class="build-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The build</span>
        <h3 class="build-title">Built from parts, not kits</h3>
        <p class="build-lead">
          Ligmax is not an assembled product: it is 31 numbered line items turned into a vessel. The hull is
          3D-printed in sections and hand-laminated in carbon fibre; the 144-cell battery pack is welded
          in-house and enclosed in its own fireproof box; rails, belts, actuators, drivers and compute are
          wired and integrated by the team.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn--primary build-cta" href="/build">See every component</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="evidence" data-reveal>
      <h3 class="evidence-title">Validated in the lab, then raced</h3>
      <p class="evidence-lead">
        Every subsystem was integrated and bench-tested before pool trials and full-course testing
        against real buoys in Trondheim and Oslo. The vessel then raced at Njord 2026, where a flooded
        hull on day one cost us the lidars and turned the week into a rebuild —
        <a href="/competition">the full account is here</a>.
      </p>
      <ul class="evidence-grid">
        {evidence.map((item) => (
          <li>
            <figure>
              <div class:list={['evidence-media', { 'evidence-media--light': item.light }]}>
                <Image
                  src={item.image}
                  alt={item.alt}
                  widths={[420, 640]}
                  sizes="(max-width: 700px) 92vw, 350px"
                />
              </div>
              <figcaption>{item.caption}</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .loops {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .loop-card {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem 1.3rem;
    border-top: 3px solid var(--brand);
  }

  .loop-number {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--blue);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .loop-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .loop-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  .features {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .feature {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .feature--flip .feature-media {
    order: 2;
  }

  .feature-media {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
  }

  .feature-media--dark {
    --carousel-caption-color: #9db8e8;
    background:
      radial-gradient(30rem 18rem at 50% 42%, rgba(120, 158, 224, 0.2), transparent 70%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--navy-900), var(--navy-800));
    border-color: var(--navy-800);
  }

  .feature-media {
    display: grid;
  }

  .media-figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .feature-media--dark .media-figure + .media-figure {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  }

  .media-figure figcaption {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding: 0.15rem 1rem 0.8rem;
  }

  .feature-media--dark .media-figure figcaption {
    color: #9db8e8;
  }

  .feature-media img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }


  .media-video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--navy-950);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .feature-eyebrow {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .feature-copy h3 {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }

  .feature-copy p {
    font-size: 1.01rem;
  }

  .feature-copy p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .build {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
    padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .build-head {
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .build-title {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .build-lead {
    color: var(--body);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .build-cta {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }

  .evidence {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
    padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .evidence-title {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .evidence-lead {
    max-width: 62ch;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  .evidence-grid {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.8rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .evidence-grid figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .evidence-media {
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--navy-900), var(--navy-800));
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
  }

  .evidence-media img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .evidence-media--light {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .evidence-media--light img {
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .evidence-grid figcaption {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1040px) {
    .loops {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .loops {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .feature {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .feature--flip .feature-media {
      order: 0;
    }

    .evidence-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      max-width: 26rem;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
